-- The demo fleet roster: the golden page's rows, the one place they live. seed.go execs it at first
-- boot of the demo compose stack and the fleet tests exec the same text. Timestamps are absolute,
-- never boot-relative; no run is left live, because the boot sweep would end it (design/EXPERIENCE.md D4).
SELECT id, 'email', who, 'owner', who, display, 'person', who, display FROM (VALUES
 ('commission-calc', 'priya@meridian.example', 'Priya Raman'), ('claims-portal', 'dana@meridian.example', 'Dana Whitfield'),
 ('claims-archive', 'tomas@meridian.example', 'Tomas Neri'), ('fnol-intake', 'marcus@meridian.example', 'Marcus Bell'),
 ('endorsement-hub', 'priya@meridian.example', 'Priya Raman'), ('premium-ledger', 'dana@meridian.example', 'Dana Whitfield')) AS o (id, who, display);
-- Production's history begins with what it runs, as the shared production writer records a promotion
-- (design/OPERATIONS.md §1.4): the next promotion's earlier[] lists the version it replaced, to put back.
SELECT project_id, package_id, image, gate_run, gate_run, deployed_at, promoted_by_kind, promoted_by_subject, promoted_by_display FROM deploys WHERE env = 'prod';
-- The verdict row as runs.Pipeline.verdict writes one: the dedupe key, and the counts at the top
-- level beside the findings. The fleet reads the findings and the gate-run routes read the other two;
-- a row shaped for one of them shows the other an unblocked run. The findings are a contract log
-- (contracts/finding.md): the story's key at its file:line, as gitleaks reports it in the golden log, because the
-- app page renders a seeded result as it renders a real one.

